# Every file in this repository is tooling text and every one of them is LF: bash
# reads the scripts on macOS and Linux, where a stray CR breaks `set -euo pipefail`,
# and the packaging hashes in dist/publish/SHA256SUMS.txt are computed over LF bytes.
# Without this, a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true yields a tree whose
# .sh files differ from the ones that were published.
* text eol=lf

# ... but "text" is a claim about every file, and since the project mark ships as a
# JPEG that claim became false: with `* text eol=lf` git rewrites CRLF byte pairs in
# the index, so a committed icon is no longer the bytes the builder baked. Binary
# types are therefore excluded explicitly, and the publish guard compares the staged
# copy against the original to catch the rest.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
